# Calendar

Show the calendar source, the local date and the time zone, and keep all-day events apart from timed ones. People mostly need the next event, so prefer a readable agenda to a grid. The shared limits for every page template are on [Page templates](index.html).

## When to use it

Adapt this structure for household calendar entries, maintenance appointments and collection schedules. Choose an agenda when the reader mainly needs the next event. Use a grid only when comparing days matters.

## Structure and behaviour

Group events by date under semantic headings, or use a table with clear headers ([WG-080](../../content/formatting-content/text-formatting.html#wg-080)). If you need a calendar grid, also provide a list alternative, and a keyboard model that does not make people tab through every empty cell. Label next and previous controls with the period they open. Name the time zone wherever a time could be read two ways ([WG-075](../../content/formatting-content/charts-and-data.html#wg-075)). Do not use colour alone for today, the selected date or event status ([WG-081](../../content/formatting-content/text-formatting.html#wg-081)).

## Home Assistant boundary

The theme does not generate schedules, infer bank holidays or create calendar entries. Keep time zone, recurrence, cancellation and permission handling with the native calendar integration, and see [Schedules, calendars and timers](../../home-assistant/schedules-and-time.html) for its states. Example dates are invented and are not household appointments.

## Household agenda

Invented appointments show a dated agenda in Europe/London. The timed visit has a GMT offset. The all-day reminder stays a calendar-date event.

